1354		Use coordinate indices $i\in\{0,\dots,m-1\}$ throughout this definition,
1355		the following mixture estimates, and the sub-line construction below. Write
1356		$\bar\chi(s)=\chi(s)-1$, where $\chi$ is the one-based index function of
1357		Definition~\ref{def:ld-question-distribution}. Thus $\bar\chi$ takes
1358		values in $\{0,\dots,m-1\}$, and index $i$ here denotes coordinate $i+1$
1359		in the one-based notation of \cite{Ji2020MIPStar}.
1360		For any such $i$, the \emph{$i$-th restricted
